A||||12||85ZainoGT||How to find codes?||||5||
Z||000000||85ZainoGT||11-13-2001||11:12 AM||||How are you supposed to find out what codes your getting?  this is probably a stupid question but oh well... I am just wondering for when my check engine light comes on? thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 Gold GT 2.8L<BR>All the options :)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SigPic2222.jpg"> <BR>NEW pics are coming SOON hopefully... geez!||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierocritter||11-13-2001||11:25 AM||||Take off the interior cover around your cigarette lighter and there is a diagnostic electrical connector to the right side of the car.(opposite of lighter) you connect two of the pin terminals(upper two towards the passenger side) with the key on. Check engine light will begin to flash codes. I have a Haynes manual and it tells you what the codes are. Hope that helps!||||reg||1
Z||000002||85ZainoGT||11-13-2001||12:09 PM||||yes helps a ton... Where and how much and what tool is it that I need to buy to take this covering off.. and just about every other covering inside the fiero?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 85ZainoGT (edited 11-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierocritter||11-13-2001||12:14 PM||||Two torx screws one on eachside!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bazooka||11-13-2001||01:05 PM||||Zaino,    To call up the "hard" codes from your ECM, you should *remove the 2 cover plate mounting screws on the Cig Lighter to gain access to the ALDL (Assembly Line Diagnostic Link). *With the "key on" and "engine off" you need to Ground the A and B terminals of the ALDL with a short Jumper wire. As soon as you do this, the diaagnostics will begin with a code 12 flashing three times successively. This will indicate that the ECM is working. *Then the codes will appear in the dash-Check Engine lite as flashes (code 23 for instance, will appear as: flash,flash----pause----flash,flash,flash). So then, if you have a code 32 you will get the following flash sequence from the dashlite ( * **   * **   * **   *** **    *** **    *** **   * **   * **   * ** ). Notice that you get (3) code 12's before and after the trouble code itself. *Record the trouble codes and disconnect the jumper. Then start up the engine and stablilize the idle. Its best to have a warmed up engine for the diagnostics. If you have multiple codes, start with the lowest numbers first as they could be activating the higher number codes.      <BR>****************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85ZainoGT:<BR>.. how do  take the cigarette outer lining deal off?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||85ZainoGT||11-13-2001||01:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Bazooka:<BR><B>Zaino,    To call up the "hard" codes from your ECM, you should *remove the 2 cover plate mounting screws on the Cig Lighter to gain access to the ALDL (Assembly Line Diagnostic Link). *With the "key on" and "engine off" you need to Ground the A and B terminals of the ALDL with a short Jumper wire. As soon as you do this, the diaagnostics will begin with a code 12 flashing three times successively. This will indicate that the ECM is working. *Then the codes will appear in the dash-Check Engine lite as flashes (code 23 for instance, will appear as: flash,flash----pause----flash,flash,flash). So then, if you have a code 32 you will get the following flash sequence from the dashlite ( * **   * **   * **   *** **    *** **    *** **   * **   * **   * ** ). Notice that you get (3) code 12's before and after the trouble code itself. *Record the trouble codes and disconnect the jumper. Then start up the engine and stablilize the idle. Its best to have a warmed up engine for the diagnostics. If you have multiple codes, start with the lowest numbers first as they could be activating the higher number codes.      <BR>****************************<BR> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>  wow... sounds REALLY confusing, hopefully its easier when I actually do it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  anyone know what tool I need to buy?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 Gold GT 2.8L<BR>All the options :)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SigPic2222.jpg"> <BR>NEW pics are coming SOON hopefully... geez!||||reg||1
Z||000006||862M4inCA||11-13-2001||02:12 PM||||After using an 8mm socket to remove the cover plate all I needed was a paperclip to check mine. works GREAT! :-D But just to be on the safe side I would ground the diagnostic terminals with the key OFF, then when you have made the connection turn it to the on position.||||reg||1
